* ===========================================================================
* MCC_TOPOLOGY_WORKSPACES.DTS
* Five purpose-built workspace postures, one per relation TOPOLOGY.
*
* Status:  CANDIDATE / REVIEW_BEFORE_EXECUTION
* Safety:  MUTATING -- writes five workspace files. No table data is touched.
* Lane:    AIF-146 (relation traversal surfaces). NOT part of the MCC
*          three-stage build chain -- it CONSUMES that chain's output, the
*          same way mcc_add_notes_memo.dts does, which is why it lives here
*          at data/scripts/ and not in data/scripts/mcc/.
* Inputs:  data/dbf/x64/*.dbf + data/indexes/x64/*.cdx  (mcc_build_x64.dts)
* Outputs: data/workspaces/topo_chain.dtschema
*          data/workspaces/topo_deep.dtschema
*          data/workspaces/topo_fan.dtschema
*          data/workspaces/topo_diamond.dtschema
*          data/workspaces/topo_flat.dtschema
* Gate:    mcc_build_x64.dts must have completed cleanly first.
*
* WHY THESE EXIST
* `enum_emit_for_current_parent` (set_relations.hpp:121) infers a chain when
* none is given by "repeatedly following the ONLY child relation at each
* step". That inference therefore SUCCEEDS on a linear graph and CANNOT
* succeed where any step has more than one child. The shipped `mcc` posture
* has fifteen relations and a three-way fan at STUDENTS, so it can never
* exercise the inference path -- it is the hard case only.
*
* These five isolate one property each, so traversal, and any future join
* surface, can be tested against a graph whose answer is known in advance
* rather than against the whole MCC graph at once.
*
* EVERY POSTURE IS WRITTEN BY `WORKSPACE SAVE`, DELIBERATELY.
* AIF-146 sec 4 and AIF-145 sec 5a: WORKSPACE SAVE writes the WORKSPACES slot
* and only that. Hand-authoring these files onto a user rung would put them
* where nothing refreshes them and where ladder 4 would never find them.
*
*   $env:X64BASE_ALLOW_DATA = "1"
*   .\datarun.ps1
*   DOTSCRIPT TRACE scripts\mcc_topology_workspaces.dts OUT tmp\topo.log
*
* Paths are INLINED rather than `DO X64` -- the DOTSCRIPT resolver resolves
* relative to the invoking script's directory, reports a miss, and CONTINUES
* with the path slots unchanged (mcc/README.md, and AIF-145 sec 4).
* ===========================================================================

SET ECHO OFF

ECHO ========================================================
ECHO MCC TOPOLOGY WORKSPACES -- five postures, five shapes
ECHO Writes workspace files only. No table data is mutated.
ECHO ========================================================

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 1of5 -- topo_chain : PURE LINEAR. One child at every step.
*         STUDENTS -> ENROLL -> CLASSES -> COURSES -> DEPT
*         5 areas, 4 relations.
* PREDICT: RELATIONS ALL shows a single unbranched spine, depth 4.
* PREDICT: chain inference SUCCEEDS here -- `REL ENUM LIMIT 5 TUPLE ...`
*          with NO explicit path emits rows, because every step has exactly
*          one child. This is the control case for the inference contract.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

WORKSPACE CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF/x64
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/x64
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/x64
ECHO [1/5] topo_chain -- STUDENTS ENROLL CLASSES COURSES DEPT

SELECT 0
USE STUDENTS
SET INDEX TO STUDENTS
SET ORDER TO TAG SID

SELECT 1
USE ENROLL
SET INDEX TO ENROLL
SET ORDER TO TAG SID

SELECT 2
USE CLASSES
SET INDEX TO CLASSES
SET ORDER TO TAG CLS_ID

SELECT 3
USE COURSES
SET INDEX TO COURSES
SET ORDER TO TAG CID

SELECT 4
USE DEPT
SET INDEX TO DEPT
SET ORDER TO TAG DEPT_ID

SELECT STUDENTS
SET RELATIONS CLEAR ALL
SET RELATIONS ADD STUDENTS ENROLL ON SID
SET RELATIONS ADD ENROLL CLASSES ON CLS_ID
SET RELATIONS ADD CLASSES COURSES ON CID
SET RELATIONS ADD COURSES DEPT ON DEPT_ID
REL REFRESH

SELECT STUDENTS
TOP
RELATIONS ALL
ECHO --- inference control: NO explicit path given ---
REL ENUM LIMIT 5 TUPLE STUDENTS.SID, ENROLL.CLS_ID, CLASSES.CID, COURSES.DEPT_ID, DEPT.DEPT_ID

WORKSPACE SAVE topo_chain
ECHO [1/5] saved topo_chain

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 2of5 -- topo_deep : LONGEST single-child path available. 5 hops.
*         STUDENTS -> ENROLL -> CLASSES -> TASSIGN -> TEACHERS -> DEPT
*         6 areas, 5 relations.
* PREDICT: inference SUCCEEDS -- still exactly one child per step.
* PREDICT: deeper than topo_chain by one hop; row counts per parent differ
*          because TASSIGN fans per class.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

WORKSPACE CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF/x64
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/x64
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/x64
ECHO [2/5] topo_deep -- STUDENTS ENROLL CLASSES TASSIGN TEACHERS DEPT

SELECT 0
USE STUDENTS
SET INDEX TO STUDENTS
SET ORDER TO TAG SID

SELECT 1
USE ENROLL
SET INDEX TO ENROLL
SET ORDER TO TAG SID

SELECT 2
USE CLASSES
SET INDEX TO CLASSES
SET ORDER TO TAG CLS_ID

SELECT 3
USE TASSIGN
SET INDEX TO TASSIGN
SET ORDER TO TAG CLS_ID

SELECT 4
USE TEACHERS
SET INDEX TO TEACHERS
SET ORDER TO TAG TID

SELECT 5
USE DEPT
SET INDEX TO DEPT
SET ORDER TO TAG DEPT_ID

SELECT STUDENTS
SET RELATIONS CLEAR ALL
SET RELATIONS ADD STUDENTS ENROLL ON SID
SET RELATIONS ADD ENROLL CLASSES ON CLS_ID
SET RELATIONS ADD CLASSES TASSIGN ON CLS_ID
SET RELATIONS ADD TASSIGN TEACHERS ON TID
SET RELATIONS ADD TEACHERS DEPT ON DEPT_ID
REL REFRESH

SELECT STUDENTS
TOP
RELATIONS ALL
ECHO --- inference: NO explicit path given ---
REL ENUM LIMIT 5 TUPLE STUDENTS.SID, ENROLL.CLS_ID, CLASSES.CID, TASSIGN.TID, TEACHERS.LNAME, DEPT.DEPT_ID

WORKSPACE SAVE topo_deep
ECHO [2/5] saved topo_deep

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 3of5 -- topo_fan : ONE parent, THREE children, depth 1.
*         STUDENTS -> ENROLL, STUD_MAJ, MAJORS
*         4 areas, 3 relations.
* PREDICT: chain inference CANNOT succeed -- step 1 has three children, so
*          there is no "only child" to follow. A bare `REL ENUM LIMIT 5` with
*          no path must NOT silently pick one.
* PREDICT: an EXPLICIT single-child path still works: `REL ENUM ENROLL ...`.
* THIS IS THE CASE TO WATCH. If the bare form emits rows anyway, it chose a
* child without being told to, and that is a finding -- an ambiguous chain
* resolved silently is the AIF-118 shape.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

WORKSPACE CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF/x64
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/x64
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/x64
ECHO [3/5] topo_fan -- STUDENTS to ENROLL, STUD_MAJ, MAJORS

SELECT 0
USE STUDENTS
SET INDEX TO STUDENTS
SET ORDER TO TAG SID

SELECT 1
USE ENROLL
SET INDEX TO ENROLL
SET ORDER TO TAG SID

SELECT 2
USE STUD_MAJ
SET INDEX TO STUD_MAJ
SET ORDER TO TAG SID

SELECT 3
USE MAJORS
SET INDEX TO MAJORS
SET ORDER TO TAG MAJOR

SELECT STUDENTS
SET RELATIONS CLEAR ALL
SET RELATIONS ADD STUDENTS ENROLL ON SID
SET RELATIONS ADD STUDENTS STUD_MAJ ON SID
SET RELATIONS ADD STUDENTS MAJORS ON MAJOR
REL REFRESH

SELECT STUDENTS
TOP
RELATIONS ALL
ECHO --- AMBIGUOUS: no path given, three children. Rows here are a FINDING. ---
REL ENUM LIMIT 5 TUPLE STUDENTS.SID, ENROLL.CLS_ID
ECHO --- EXPLICIT single child: this one SHOULD emit ---
REL ENUM ENROLL LIMIT 5 TUPLE STUDENTS.SID, ENROLL.CLS_ID

WORKSPACE SAVE topo_fan
ECHO [3/5] saved topo_fan

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 4of5 -- topo_diamond : TWO paths converge on one node.
*         STUDENTS -> MAJORS        (direct, ON MAJOR)
*         STUDENTS -> STUD_MAJ      (ON SID)
*         STUD_MAJ -> MAJORS        (ON MAJOR)
*         3 areas, 3 relations. MAJORS is reachable two ways.
* PREDICT: RELATIONS ALL renders MAJORS TWICE -- once per path -- because the
*          tree builder walks paths, not nodes.
* PREDICT: STUDENTS has two children, so bare inference cannot proceed here
*          either; the explicit form `REL ENUM STUD_MAJ MAJORS ...` is the
*          one that names the longer arm.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

WORKSPACE CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF/x64
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/x64
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/x64
ECHO [4/5] topo_diamond -- two paths from STUDENTS to MAJORS

SELECT 0
USE STUDENTS
SET INDEX TO STUDENTS
SET ORDER TO TAG SID

SELECT 1
USE STUD_MAJ
SET INDEX TO STUD_MAJ
SET ORDER TO TAG SID

SELECT 2
USE MAJORS
SET INDEX TO MAJORS
SET ORDER TO TAG MAJOR

SELECT STUDENTS
SET RELATIONS CLEAR ALL
SET RELATIONS ADD STUDENTS MAJORS ON MAJOR
SET RELATIONS ADD STUDENTS STUD_MAJ ON SID
SET RELATIONS ADD STUD_MAJ MAJORS ON MAJOR
REL REFRESH

SELECT STUDENTS
TOP
RELATIONS ALL
ECHO --- explicit long arm ---
REL ENUM STUD_MAJ MAJORS LIMIT 5 TUPLE STUDENTS.SID, STUD_MAJ.MAJOR, MAJORS.DEPT_ID

WORKSPACE SAVE topo_diamond
ECHO [4/5] saved topo_diamond

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 5of5 -- topo_flat : areas open, ZERO relations.
*         STUDENTS, ENROLL, CLASSES, DEPT. 4 areas, 0 relations.
* PREDICT: RELATIONS ALL reports no relations from the current root.
* PREDICT: this is the shape `WORKSPACE SAVE` produces after a plain
*          `WORKSPACE OPEN DBF` -- which is exactly why the shipped
*          mcc_x64 posture carries 0 relations (AIF-145 sec 5a). This posture
*          makes that the DELIBERATE floor case rather than an accident.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

WORKSPACE CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF/x64
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/x64
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/x64
ECHO [5/5] topo_flat -- four areas, no relations

SELECT 0
USE STUDENTS
SET INDEX TO STUDENTS
SET ORDER TO TAG SID

SELECT 1
USE ENROLL
SET INDEX TO ENROLL
SET ORDER TO TAG SID

SELECT 2
USE CLASSES
SET INDEX TO CLASSES
SET ORDER TO TAG CLS_ID

SELECT 3
USE DEPT
SET INDEX TO DEPT
SET ORDER TO TAG DEPT_ID

SELECT STUDENTS
SET RELATIONS CLEAR ALL
REL REFRESH

SELECT STUDENTS
TOP
RELATIONS ALL

WORKSPACE SAVE topo_flat
ECHO [5/5] saved topo_flat

* ===========================================================================
* PROOF
* ===========================================================================
* A green run is not proof. Read these five things:
*
*   1. topo_chain and topo_deep: the BARE `REL ENUM` (no path) EMITTED ROWS.
*      If it did not, chain inference does not work on a linear graph and the
*      contract at set_relations.hpp:121 is wrong.
*   2. topo_fan: the BARE `REL ENUM` emitted NOTHING and said why. Rows there
*      mean a child was chosen silently -- report it, do not work around it.
*   3. topo_fan: the EXPLICIT `REL ENUM ENROLL` DID emit.
*   4. topo_diamond: RELATIONS ALL showed MAJORS twice, once per path.
*   5. Five `WORKSPACE SAVE` lines all reported success, and the five files
*      landed in data\workspaces -- NOT under dottalkpp\user\. If any landed
*      on a user rung, AIF-145 sec 5a is wrong about the write path and that
*      is the more important finding.
* ===========================================================================

ECHO ========================================================
ECHO TOPOLOGY WORKSPACES COMPLETE -- five postures written.
ECHO
ECHO   WORKSPACE LOAD topo_chain     linear, inference works
ECHO   WORKSPACE LOAD topo_deep      linear, 5 hops
ECHO   WORKSPACE LOAD topo_fan       3-way fan, inference must refuse
ECHO   WORKSPACE LOAD topo_diamond   two paths to one node
ECHO   WORKSPACE LOAD topo_flat      areas only, no relations
ECHO
ECHO Verify where they landed:
ECHO   dir dottalkpp\data\workspaces\topo_*.dtschema
ECHO   dir dottalkpp\user\default\workspaces\topo_*.dtschema   (expect none)
ECHO ========================================================
